obscure	one
constantly_treated	one
fix_meaning	one
# "necessary" occurs in two senses in S1: "necessary connexion" (a causal tie) and "every moment necessary for us" (unavoidable for the inquirer). But each sense stays inside a different claim and is used the same way wherever that claim appears.
# A1 links the obscurity of the ideas to the obscurity of this species of philosophy. "Obscure" means unclear or ill-defined in both places; only what is obscure differs. So A1 joins different claims, not two senses of one word, and is not a bridge.
